{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>You shall do no injustice in judgment.</b> That one party not be treated gently and another harshly — one standing and another seated, and all similar cases. After this he states the failing that befalls those between the judges and the leaders of the people, namely hatred and slander to the king, in the manner of Doeg and his associates, who informed against David to Saul (1 Samuel 22:9). From this there follows the pursuit of bloodshed, vengeance, and bearing a grudge, as the prophet testified, saying: אַנְשֵׁי רָכִיל הָיוּ בָךְ לְמַעַן שְׁפָךְ דָם (Ezekiel 22:9). Concerning all of these he gives a general principle, saying:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:58.326536141Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}